10-8-26:
    ✔ Add React Query (TanStack Query v5) for server state — why (discussed 2026-10-05): it does NOT make a request faster (measured: one Atlas query takes 200–2,000 ms, every request costs two of them because protect looks the user up, and Home / Orders load rounds first, then one GET /orders per round); what it does give: switching tabs shows the last data at once while it refreshes in the background (today every tab shows "Loading…" for 1–2 s), a save refreshes the related lists right away instead of on the next 7s poll, less hand-written loading code, and a library juniors are asked about; the real-latency fixes (Atlas region, one request instead of one per round) are separate, optional tasks @done(26-10-08 21:28)
        ✔ 1. Decisions (Jui, 2026-10-08: all as proposed) — proposed defaults, confirm or change each: (a) staleTime 0 + cache kept 5 min — a tab shows its cached data instantly and always refetches behind it; (b) lists keep polling every 7s with refetchInterval, and stop while the app is in the background (React Query's default — saves battery, and it refetches the moment the phone comes back to it); (c) refetchOnWindowFocus ON for lists (coming back from LINE shows fresh orders at once) but OFF for edit pages; (d) edit pages (EditOrder / EditRestock / EditStockItem / EditExpense) keep "loaded once, can't change underfoot": useQuery with staleTime Infinity and no refetching, and the form state is filled from it once; (e) retry 1 instead of the default 3 — with Atlas this slow, 3 retries with back-off would leave "Loading…" up for ~10 s before an error shows; (f) saves go through useMutation and then invalidateQueries for the lists they affect (e.g. a new order → orders + stock-items + finances summary, since it deducts stock and adds revenue); (g) the full-page error only when there's no data yet (isError && !data), like usePolling — a failed refresh keeps the last data on screen; (h) add @tanstack/react-query-devtools, development only, to see the cache while learning; (i) Zustand: React Query covers the server data, which is nearly all the app's state, so drop Zustand from the "intended direction" in CLAUDE.md unless a real client-only need shows up @done(26-10-08)
        ✔ 2. Client: npm install @tanstack/react-query (+ @tanstack/react-query-devtools as a devDependency per 1h); one QueryClient with the defaults from step 1 in src/main.jsx, <QueryClientProvider> around <App />; check it works with the React Compiler and StrictMode (no manual memoization needed) — v5.104; devtools are left out of the production build (checked); the bundle grew 88.7 → 108.8 kB gzip @done(26-10-08)
        ✔ 3. Client: src/queries.js — every query key and fetch function in one place, so a key can't be typed two different ways (the classic invalidation bug) — built with plural roots for lists (['rounds', 'active', 'earnings'] Home, ['rounds', 'with-orders'] Orders, ['rounds', 'active'] New order, ['stock-items'], ['stock-items', 'with-deleted'], ['restocks'], ['finances']) and singular roots for one document (['order', id], ['stock-item', id], ['restock', id], ['expense', id]) so refreshing a list never refetches the edit page that's deleting its document; presets POLLED / FORM_LIST / LOAD_ONCE (gcTime 0: an edit page never reopens on an old cached copy); AFFECTED_BY says which lists each kind of save refreshes; refreshAfterSave refetches them (refetchType 'all', awaited) before the page navigates; fetch functions reuse getJson (401 → logout() unchanged); Home's and Orders' "rounds, then orders per round" stay one query each (same requests as before) @done(26-10-08)
        ✔ 4. Client: the polled list pages — Stock (now two queries, so Home and Stock share the ['stock-items'] cache), Finances, Orders, Home (rounds + stock with select: pickPreviewItems) — useQuery + refetchInterval; the full-page error only shows with no data yet; End round drops the row with setQueryData, then refreshes the rounds lists @done(26-10-08)
        ✔ 5. Client: the one-off loads — NewOrder's rounds (the single-round auto-pick is now worked out each render instead of set in an effect) and Restock's names use FORM_LIST; the four edit pages are split into a loader (useQuery + LOAD_ONCE) and a …Form component that starts its fields with useState(data.x) — no more useEffect + setX; EditRestock waits for its item list too, as before @done(26-10-08)
        ✔ 6. Client: every save is a useMutation whose mutationFn saves and then awaits refreshAfterSave; the status radio keeps its optimistic update (onMutate / revert in onError) and refreshes without waiting since it stays on the page; isPending replaced the hand-written isSubmitting flags @done(26-10-08)
        ✔ 7. Client: deleted hooks/usePolling.js (nothing imports it); lint + build pass @done(26-10-08)
        ✔ 8. Test (Playwright at 390px + Jui on two phones): switching Home → Orders → Stock → Finances and back shows data instantly the second time (time it before and after — a number for the PR and the portfolio); lists still update within 7s when the other phone changes something; after each save the target list already shows the change on arrival, with no wait; edit pages never reset what's being typed; first-load error and Try again still work (stop the API server to test); 401 still logs out; Devtools shows the expected keys; no console errors — Playwright part done 2026-10-08 (Jui's two-phone check still open): tab switch (measured until the new page's subtitle shows and "Loading…" is gone, 3 rounds each) went from 183–575 ms with "Loading…" every time to 8–20 ms with no "Loading…" from the second visit on (first visits 98–211 ms); after saving a round / order / restock / expense, Home / Orders / Stock / Finances already showed it on arrival (save → arrival 229–573 ms); a new order's deduction (Churro 50 → 46) and revenue (฿1,182 → ฿1,241) were on Stock / Finances right away, cancelling put them back; End round dropped the row in ~100 ms; EditOrder's status changed on tap, and a note typed on the page survived 9.5 s plus focus / visibility events with only one GET; reopening an edit page after a change from "the other phone" showed the new value (gcTime 0), not the cached one; delete / cancel never flashed "not found" / "cancelled" before leaving; Edit stock item sent only the changed field; a change made from a script showed on Stock within one 7s poll; with the API blocked, Stock showed "Cannot reach the server" + Try again after 1.6 s and Try again loaded it; no console errors besides the blocked requests; all ZZ test data removed and stock restored to the snapshot. Note for testing: React Router changes the URL before it renders the new page, so wait for the page's own content, not location.pathname @done(26-10-08 21:28)
        ✔ 9. Docs: CLAUDE.md — Structure (React Query is the state library; usePolling gone; src/queries.js), the polling notes (refetchInterval instead of usePolling), Zustand dropped per 1i @done(26-10-08)
    ✔ Tab switch animation (branch feat/animations — more animations from Jui's own design may follow on it) — decided 2026-10-08: the brown pill slides to the new tab and the page's content fades in (not in the design; Jui picked this over a direction-based slide or pill-only); built with plain CSS, not View Transitions (those lift the named pill above the page, so it would cover the tab labels while sliding): AppShell remembers the last tab in a module-level object (each page renders its own AppShell, so the nav is new on every switch), draws one absolutely-positioned pill at the old tab and moves it on the next frame (translateX, 200ms ease-out); labels are coloured by the pill's position so they turn white as it arrives; <main> uses a new animate-fade-in (200ms, @theme in index.css), which plays because main mounts afresh on each switch — only the new content fades in, the old page disappears at once (fading it out too would need keeping it on screen, e.g. View Transitions); both are off with prefers-reduced-motion; tested with Playwright at 390px: Home → Stock the pill went 4 → 175 px through in-between positions in ~200ms and landed exactly on the Stock tab, content opacity rose 0 → 1, Stock label white / 600, aria-current on Stock; opening /orders directly and coming back from an edit page did not slide; with reduced motion the pill jumped and nothing faded; looks the same as before at rest; lint, build, no console errors @done(26-10-08)
    ✔ Round open / close animation on Orders (feat/animations, Jui 2026-10-08 — the design opens and closes instantly) — the panel slides open / shut and fades, 200ms ease-out like the tab switch; the chevron's turn went 150 → 200ms to match; done with a one-row CSS grid going 0fr ↔ 1fr (CSS can't animate height: auto), so the panel is now always rendered and gets `inert` while closed (no Tab / screen-reader access to hidden rows); the header button gained aria-expanded; the header's bottom border still switches instantly (a transparent one would add 1px to closed rounds); a round opened by defaultOpen (just placed an order) starts open without animating; tested with Playwright at 390px: open 0 → 291 px and opacity 0 → 1 in ~180ms, close back to 0 the same way, a closed card is still 48px (header only), Tab never reached a closed round's links, Enter opens it and Tab then reaches the "All" chip, filters still work, a round stays open and steady through a 7s poll, defaultOpen shows full height from the first frame, reduced motion opens / closes instantly, no console errors @done(26-10-08)
    ✔ End round animation on Home (feat/animations, Jui 2026-10-09 picked "slide out left + close up" over fade + close up / close up only — the design removes the row instantly) — once the server has ended the round, the card slides out to the left (the way it was swiped) and fades while its row closes up, 200ms, so the rows and "Start a new round" below move up smoothly; new: while the PATCH is on its way the button reads "Ending…" and is disabled (before, nothing showed the tap had worked for 100–600ms); Home's mutation no longer drops the row itself — RoundRow calls onGone after the slide (a timer, since transitionend never fires with reduced motion), which removes it from the cache and only then refreshes the rounds lists, so a refetch can't pull it away mid-slide; a failed PATCH leaves the row as before; the 8px between rows moved from the list's flex gap into each row (pb-2) so it closes up with the row instead of jumping; lesson: Tailwind v4's translate-* utilities set the CSS translate property, so the transition must list translate, not transform (the first version faded but didn't slide); tested with Playwright at 390px on throwaway ZZ rounds: spacing unchanged (rows 52px, 8px between rows / to the button / under the heading), "Ending…" + disabled while waiting, then x 0 → -100%, opacity 1 → 0 and height 60 → 0 in ~180ms with the button below moving up 60px steadily, the row gone and the round ended in Atlas; a blocked PATCH kept the row, put the button back and showed "Cannot reach the server"; reduced motion removed the row at once; test rounds removed @done(26-10-09)
10-12-26:
    ✔ Pre-deploy security (branch chore/pre-deploy-security) — from the security review of 2026-10-12; "totalPrice is trusted from the client" (any logged-in person can set an order's total) is NOT fixed here — Jui: not yet, fine while only Jui and Impact have accounts; recheck if a third account is ever added @done(26-10-14)
        ✔ 1. Decisions (Jui, 2026-10-12): JWT — a new random secret + a tokenVersion on each account + tokens last 30 days (not 90), over shorter-only expiry / sliding expiry / access + refresh tokens (the last is more than two people need); Log out bumps tokenVersion too, so it really ends the session on the server — and logs that account out on every phone it's signed in on; production gets its own database and starts empty (accounts and starting stock created with the seed scripts — no sign-up page: a public sign-up would let anyone in to see orders and money) @done(26-10-12)
        ✔ 2. Server: login refuses anything but strings — `typeof email !== 'string' || typeof password !== 'string'` → 400 before the query. Confirmed in the review: { "email": { "$gt": "" } } matched the first account without knowing any email (only the password then stood in the way), and a password sent as an object made bcrypt throw a 500. Also lower-case the email before looking it up (the model stores it lower-case, so "Jui@…" can't log in today). Test: operator email → 400, object password → 400, mixed-case email + right password → logs in — done: operator email and object password → 400 (the object used to be a 500), "JUI@…" logs in @done(26-10-12)
        ✔ 3. Server: rate-limit POST /users/login with express-rate-limit (e.g. 10 tries per 15 min per IP, the 429 message in the same JSON shape as AppError); add app.set('trust proxy', 1) — hosts like Render / Railway sit behind a proxy, and without it every visitor shares the proxy's IP, so one person's failed tries would lock everyone out. Test: the 11th wrong try → 429, a right password after the window → works — done: express-rate-limit 8 in routes/userRoutes.js (10 failed tries / 15 min / IP, skipSuccessfulRequests, 429 through errorController, RateLimit headers); malformed attempts count as failures too; trust proxy only when NODE_ENV=production — with no proxy in front, trusting X-Forwarded-For would let anyone fake their IP past the limit @done(26-10-12)
        ✔ 4. Server: JWT — tokenVersion (Number, default 0) on User; signToken puts it in the token; protect rejects a token whose version doesn't match the account's (401, so apiFetch logs out as today) — no extra query, protect already loads the user; JWT_EXPIRES_IN 90d → 30d; new POST /users/logout (behind protect) does $inc tokenVersion. Client: logout() calls it, then removes the token and goes to /login as now — even if the call fails (offline), so nobody gets stuck on Home. Test: log out → the old token gets 401; a second token for the same account (the "other phone") also stops working; the other person's account is unaffected; an account saved before the field existed (no tokenVersion) still logs in — done: token payload { id, v }, protect → 401 "Your session has ended" on a version mismatch, POST /users/logout (), client api.js split into endSession() (local, used by apiFetch on 401) and logout() (server call with a 5s timeout, then endSession); tested: 30-day token, logout ends both of the account's tokens, the other account unaffected, an account without the field still works, logout without a token → 401; in the browser the old token got 200 before Log out and 401 after @done(26-10-12)
        ✔ 5. Server: a new random JWT_SECRET for development now (node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(64).toString('hex'))") — today's is 37 characters but only 15 different ones, guessable offline from any one leaked token; everyone logs in once more; production gets its own, different secret (step 11) — done: 128 hex characters (512 bits) written by a script that never printed it; JWT_EXPIRES_IN=30d; Jui logged in again @done(26-10-12)
        ✔ 6. Server: CORS only for the app's own address — cors({ origin: process.env.CLIENT_ORIGIN }) with CLIENT_ORIGIN in config.env (http://localhost:5173 in development); today any website can call the API. Test: a request with another Origin gets no Access-Control-Allow-Origin header; the app still works — done: CLIENT_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173 in config.env, app.js throws at start if it is missing (an unset origin would make cors() allow everyone); another Origin gets no Allow-Origin header, the app does @done(26-10-12)
        ✔ 7. Server: errorController before going live (Jui 2026-10-05 left the dev behaviour "until deploy") — ValidationError / CastError / duplicate key → 400 with a short message in every environment; anything other than development is treated as production (today an unset NODE_ENV sends no response and the request hangs); development still adds the stack. Test with NODE_ENV unset, development and production: a bad amount → 400, a bad id → 400, an unknown error → 500 "Something went very wrong" without details outside development — done: toKnownError() maps JWT / CastError / 11000 / ValidationError / broken JSON / oversized body in every environment; development adds the stack; anything but development is treated as production, so nothing hangs any more; handleDuplicateFields no longer crashes when keyValue is missing; tested with NODE_ENV development / production / unset @done(26-10-12)
        ✔ 8. Server: helmet() for the standard security headers (one line); npm audit fix in server/ and client/ (proxy-addr is critical once trust proxy is on in step 3; morgan, qs, source-map-js) — check nothing breaks; remove the deprecated npm "crypto" package from server/package.json (Node has crypto built in) and the unused crypto import in authController — done: helmet 8 (nosniff, CSP, no X-Powered-By), npm audit fix → 0 vulnerabilities in server/ and client/, crypto package and its unused import removed; note: after the client audit fix, a tab opened before it crashed once with "Invalid hook call" (Vite re-optimised its deps, the page mixed two React copies) — a reload fixes it, dev server only @done(26-10-12)
        ✔ 9. Scripts (server/scripts/, gitignored) ready for production: seedAccount.js and seedStock.js read the env file named in ENV_FILE (default config.env), e.g. ENV_FILE=config.prod.env node scripts/seedAccount.js Jui <email>; add config.*.env to .gitignore (only config.env is ignored today, so a config.prod.env could slip into git); seedAccount asks for the password with hidden typing instead of taking it on the command line (it stays in the terminal's history today) and requires 12+ characters; both print which database they're about to write to, so dev and production can't be mixed up — done: shared scripts/scriptEnv.js (loadEnv, confirmDatabase, a hidden-input prompt); both scripts print the env file and database and need a y; seedAccount takes <name> <email> and asks the password twice, hidden, 12+ characters; server/config.*.env ignored; tested by piping input: missing env file, too short, mismatch, N → nothing written, one real zz-seed account (stored as a $2b$12$ bcrypt hash) then deleted @done(26-10-12)
        ✔ 10. Test everything above together: lint / build; Playwright with Jui logged in — log in, use each tab, save something, log out → back to /login and the old token refused; the app keeps working from http://localhost:5173 with CORS on — done: scratchpad securityTest.js ran app.js on port 3999 (its own rate-limit store) with two throwaway ZZ accounts, in development / production / unset NODE_ENV — all checks passed (the limiter blocked after 10 failed requests counting the two malformed ones, as intended); client lint + build pass; Playwright: every tab loads with CORS + helmet on, Log out → POST 200, token gone, old token 401, /finances without a token redirects to /login, no console errors @done(26-10-12)
        ✔ 11. Deploy settings (done on the host and in Atlas, not in code) — a checklist for deploy day: NODE_ENV=production; HTTPS on both sides and VITE_API_URL starting with https://; every variable set in the host's dashboard (never upload config.env); production's own JWT_SECRET and CLIENT_ORIGIN (the frontend's real address); a new Atlas database (e.g. churo-ops-prod) with its own database user that can only readWrite that database (not an admin), with a long random password — Network Access will likely need 0.0.0.0/0 because free hosts have no fixed IP, so that password is what protects the data; Jui and Impact's production passwords 12+ characters and not reused; seed the two accounts and the starting stock with the step 9 scripts; plan regular exports, since free Atlas has no automatic backup — the step-by-step version for Vercel + Railway is under 10-13-26 Deploy — done there @done(26-10-14)
        ✔ 12. Docs: CLAUDE.md — auth (tokenVersion, 30d, server-side Log out, rate limit), errorController no longer "left as is", CORS / helmet / trust proxy, the scripts' ENV_FILE, deploy checklist; also drop the stale "more animations may follow on the feat/animations branch" line (that branch is merged and deleted) — done: CLAUDE.md auth / server notes / known gaps / scripts updated, stale feat/animations line removed @done(26-10-12)
10-13-26:
    ✔ Deploy (branch chore/deploy) — frontend on Vercel, backend on Railway, database on the production Atlas cluster @done(26-10-14)
        ✔ 1. Decisions (Jui, 2026-10-13): frontend on Vercel (just static files, so it can move to another static host later); backend on Railway (~$5/month, doesn't sleep) over Render free (sleeps after 15 min idle, ~1 min to wake — the first order of the day would wait) and Render Starter ($7); not Express on Vercel — serverless would reset the login rate limit's memory store and reconnect to Atlas on cold starts @done(26-10-13)
        ✔ 2. Atlas production (Jui, 2026-10-13): a separate Atlas project with its own free cluster, database churo-ops-prod, its own database user; server/config.prod.env filled in except CLIENT_ORIGIN (gitignored; checked by a script that printed no values: all 7 variables, <db_password> + churo-ops-prod in DATABASE, a different host from dev, its own 128-character JWT_SECRET); seeded and checked: Jui's account (bcrypt 12, tokenVersion 0, unique email index) and the 5 starting stock items at 0 with their auto-deduct rules (unique name index, strength 2) @done(26-10-13)
        ✔ 3. Seed Impact's account (Impact types their own password): $env:ENV_FILE = 'config.prod.env'; node scripts/seedAccount.js Impact <email>; Remove-Item Env:ENV_FILE — check the script says churo-ops-prod before answering y @done(26-10-14 00:19)
        ✔ 4. Server: a start command Railway can run — `npm start` is `nodemon server.js`, but nodemon isn't in package.json (it's installed globally on Jui's PC), so Railway would crash with "nodemon: not found"; and nodemon restarts on file changes, which production doesn't need. Proposal: "start": "node server.js" (what Railway runs), "dev": "nodemon server.js" (Jui runs npm run dev in server/ from now on, like client/); drop start:prod and cross-env (production's NODE_ENV comes from Railway's variables); add "engines": { "node": "24.x" } so Railway builds with the same Node as Jui's PC — needs Jui's OK, it changes the everyday command — done (Jui OK'd 2026-10-13): "start": "node server.js", engines node 24.x, start:prod and cross-env removed (server audit 0); "dev" is "node --watch server.js" instead of nodemon — adding nodemon as a devDependency brought 3 high audit warnings (chokidar → braces) whose only "fix" was nodemon 1.x, and Node 24 has the same restart-on-change built in; tested: npm start listens with no nodemon, npm run dev serves and restarts after a file change @done(26-10-13)
        ✔ 5. Server: the login rate limit's IP on Railway — Railway's edge sets X-Real-IP to the visitor's IP, but the number of proxies in front of the app can vary, so `trust proxy` 1 may give a Railway proxy's IP instead of the visitor's: then everyone shares one limit (10 typos by anyone lock out both phones). Proposal: in production the login limiter keys on X-Real-IP (through express-rate-limit's ipKeyGenerator for IPv6), keep trust proxy 1 for the rest; check after deploy — needs Jui's OK — done (Jui OK'd 2026-10-13): clientIp(req) in routes/userRoutes.js, keyGenerator: ipKeyGenerator(clientIp(req)); tested on port 3999 with no database (password-less logins → 400, which count as failures): production — one X-Real-IP blocked at the 11th, another X-Real-IP still allowed, a changing X-Forwarded-For didn't get round it, IPv6 addresses in one /56 shared a count, no header → falls back to req.ip; development — a changing X-Real-IP was ignored (429 at the 11th); no ERR_ERL validation errors. Still to see on Railway itself (step 9) @done(26-10-13)
        ✔ 6. Client: client/vercel.json rewriting every path to /index.html — without it, opening /orders directly or refreshing any page but Home is a Vercel 404 (React Router only runs once index.html has loaded) — done: { "rewrites": [{ "source": "/(.*)", "destination": "/index.html" }] } (Vercel serves real files like /assets/* first); lint + build pass; the refresh itself can only be checked on Vercel (step 9) @done(26-10-13)
        ✔ 7. Railway: New project → Deploy from GitHub repo → Root Directory server; Variables: NODE_ENV, DATABASE, DATABASE_PASSWORD, JWT_SECRET, JWT_EXPIRES_IN from config.prod.env (copy each value, no spaces or newline at the end) — not PORT, Railway sets it; CLIENT_ORIGIN after step 8; Networking → Generate Domain → the backend's https address; Atlas Network Access → 0.0.0.0/0 (Railway has no fixed outgoing IP), so the database user's password is what protects the data; the deploy log shows "DB connection successful!"; https://<backend>/api/v1/rounds without a token → 401 JSON — done by Jui (2026-10-14): deployed backend first, with CLIENT_ORIGIN set to the expected Vercel address (the server refuses to start without one, and it only needs a restart to change — VITE_API_URL needs a rebuild, so the frontend is the one that gets the real value); "DB connection successful!" in the log, /api/v1/rounds → 401 @done(26-10-14)
        ✔ 8. Vercel: Add New Project → import the repo → Root Directory client (framework Vite, build npm run build, output dist); project name = the address (<name>.vercel.app); Environment Variable VITE_API_URL = the Railway https address, no / at the end; deploy; open the site and run location.origin in the console → put it in CLIENT_ORIGIN on Railway (and in config.prod.env as a record) → Railway redeploys; VITE_API_URL is baked in at build time, so changing it later needs a Vercel redeploy — done by Jui (2026-10-14): logged in, every tab loaded the seeded stock, refreshing /stock didn't 404, no CORS errors; config.prod.env's CLIENT_ORIGIN still to be filled in as a record (the live value is on Railway) @done(26-10-14)
