        ✔ 10. Backups: free Atlas has none — a mongodump of churo-ops-prod to Jui's PC (e.g. weekly), and a restore tried once so it's known to work — done (Jui 2026-10-14: our own Node scripts rather than installing mongodump, run by hand once a week, files outside the repo): server/scripts/backupDb.js (gitignored, ENV_FILE like the seed scripts, read-only so no y/N) saves each collection as canonical EJSON (keeps ObjectId / Date types — plain JSON would break the references) plus _meta.json with counts and indexes into D:\Backups\churo-ops\<date-time>-<db>\ (BACKUP_DIR to change; refuses a folder inside the repo), then reads every file back; restoreDb.js <folder> [--db <name>] restores only into an empty database (never overwrites or deletes), asks y/N, creates indexes before inserting; practice run: production backed up, restored into churo-ops-restore-test on the dev cluster — every document identical (types included), indexes identical, the unique stock name ("CHURRO") and email refused duplicates, N wrote nothing, a second restore was refused (not empty), an in-repo BACKUP_DIR was refused; bug found and fixed: empty collections weren't created; practice database dropped. Backups hold both accounts' emails and password hashes — never upload them anywhere public. Do one more practice restore once real orders exist (references between rounds / orders / stock not yet exercised) @done(26-10-14)
